---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Compliance Crosswalk — AI Red Team Framework"
  description="How AI red team engagements satisfy ISO/IEC 42001, NIST AI RMF, EU AI Act, OSFI E-21, NYDFS 500."
>
  <section class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6 lg:px-8 py-12">
    <p class="text-sm font-medium text-accent-700">Compliance</p>
    <h1 class="font-display font-semibold text-3xl md:text-4xl tracking-tight text-ink-900 mt-2">Compliance crosswalk</h1>
    <p class="mt-3 text-ink-600">How engagement output satisfies the testing requirements of major frameworks.</p>

    <div class="prose prose-lg max-w-prose-wide mt-8">
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Framework</th>
            <th>Requirement</th>
            <th>Engagement output produced</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>ISO/IEC 42001</td><td>Clause 8.3 / 9.1 — evaluation</td><td>Per-engagement test reports</td></tr>
          <tr><td>NIST AI RMF</td><td>MEASURE-2.7 — adversarial testing</td><td>Per-engagement test reports</td></tr>
          <tr><td>EU AI Act</td><td>Article 15 — accuracy, robustness, cybersecurity</td><td>High-risk system test reports</td></tr>
          <tr><td>OSFI E-21</td><td>Operational resilience testing</td><td>Compliance-driven engagement output</td></tr>
          <tr><td>NYDFS Part 500</td><td>§500.05 — penetration testing</td><td>Engagement output where in scope</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <p>For more depth see <a href="/playbook/12-compliance-mapping">Playbook chapter 12</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
